# Domain tests

When adding, changing, or removing behavior, update tests in the same domain, then run that domain's suite before finishing. Cover the new path and nearby edges (tags, grouping, amounts, dates). Docs-only edits do not need a test run.

| Touched paths | Command |
|---|---|
| `src/**` | `CI=true npm test -- --watchAll=false` |
| `functions/**` | `npm test --prefix functions` |
| `appScript/**` | `node --test appScript/*.test.js` |

A change that spans domains runs each matching command. Do not skip existing tests. Do not call live Firebase, Gmail, or Gemini in unit tests.

- React: grouping, search, budgets, duplicate visibility, merge math, and UI for Duplicate Review / Merge / Tag / Edit Budget.
- Functions: `detect`, survivor/tag merge, scan filters. Keep synthetic fixtures in-repo; skip the gitignored dump when missing.
- Apps Script: Gemini shape, bank match, HTML extract, UPI/vendor/tag, validation retry, quiet hours.
